>>
Rule 1 (x and y must have the same dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (x and y must be broadcast-compatible along trailing dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = (if i < ndim(v_2) then shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) else 1) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) = 1 ∨ (if i < ndim(v_2) then shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) else 1) = 1)) ∨ (ndim(v_2) ≥ ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : (shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) = (if i < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) else 1) ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1 - i) = 1 ∨ (if i < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1 - i) else 1) = 1))
>>
Rule 3 (all tensor shape dimensions are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, j) ≥ 0)
>>
Rule 4 (name is an unconstrained string parameter)
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = v_1
